{"h":2857,"lines":[{"x":0.077854670476447674,"y":0.061046511363505251,"c":1,"h":0.014534884186538477,"t":"Introduction","w":0.10553633371988932},{"y":0.10794975356026959,"c":1,"w":0.071433130900065117,"h":0.02061091610566157,"t":"Writing","x":0.080327682435585052},{"h":0.022327792819685777,"x":0.079461470288028024,"y":0.13111508504275549,"t":"This test consists of two tasks. It is suggested that candidates spend about 20 minutes on","w":0.70958582560221362,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"Task 1, which requires them to write at least 150 words, and 40 minutes on Task 2, which","x":0.079539578877388425,"y":0.15096788885411394,"w":0.70079233805338548,"h":0.020679291017077217},{"t":"requires them to write at least 250 words. Task 2 contributes twice as much as Task 1 to the","w":0.72514790852864586,"c":1,"y":0.16803678821827106,"x":0.079469522209211149,"h":0.021871582789384392},{"x":0.080900198625853931,"w":0.11330521901448568,"c":1,"h":0.017854132628924768,"t":"Writing score.","y":0.19077500774190348},{"t":"Task 1 requires candidates to look at a diagram or some data (in a graph, table or chart)","h":0.020364634551895189,"c":1,"y":0.20598013036317198,"w":0.69733373006184896,"x":0.098572705540319799},{"y":0.22321439074537297,"w":0.68701044718424487,"x":0.081230254943348498,"c":1,"t":"and to present the information in their own words. They are assessed on their ability to","h":0.02122611612436065},{"t":"organise, present and possibly compare data, and are required to describe the stages of a","x":0.081220603819851925,"w":0.71471745808919263,"h":0.021655765423998385,"y":0.24179528666666106,"c":1},{"x":0.081186418355122303,"w":0.56075525919596358,"c":1,"t":"process, describe an object or event, or explain how something works.","h":0.021934735516387249,"y":0.26044104227705844},{"c":1,"t":"In Task 2, candidates are presented with a point of view, argument or problem. They","y":0.27951226084568892,"x":0.096840479335848315,"w":0.67138219197591154,"h":0.020190551950015512},{"h":0.01991508689437238,"w":0.69044489542643228,"t":"are assessed on their ability to present a solution to the problem, present and justify an","x":0.081246428305173118,"y":0.29783694678699379,"c":1},{"x":0.081242387217378684,"h":0.021008701738233326,"c":1,"y":0.31632745671007201,"w":0.70774022420247396,"t":"opinion, compare and contrast evidence and opinions, and evaluate and challenge ideas,"},{"y":0.33685549416563831,"w":0.19065139770507813,"c":1,"t":"evidence or arguments.","x":0.081162897386070326,"h":0.017121769482643989},{"c":1,"t":"Candidates are also assessed on their ability to write in an appropriate style. More","x":0.10034600971698988,"y":0.35465116286486809,"w":0.650519053141276,"h":0.015988371937820545},{"w":0.68529805501302088,"h":0.021833792193274748,"t":"information on assessing the Writing test, including Writing assessment criteria (public","c":1,"x":0.079500096963065703,"y":0.37048081833426116},{"x":0.081314880335483883,"y":0.39244186017292648,"c":1,"h":0.01744186102384615,"t":"version), is available at ielts.org.","w":0.25432525634765624},{"h":0.01744186102384615,"y":0.42441860434822776,"x":0.081314878030192786,"c":1,"t":"Speaking","w":0.088235295613606754},{"y":0.44751574502405522,"t":"This test takes between 11 and 14 minutes and is conducted by a trained examiner.","h":0.016147045591980325,"x":0.08131488248010238,"w":0.66262975056966145,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"There are three parts:","x":0.081037479716799019,"y":0.46628758335727261,"w":0.17535657246907554,"h":0.018544507410411137},{"t":"Part 1","h":0.014534882851794828,"y":0.49709302350869555,"w":0.050173009236653632,"c":1,"x":0.08304498368184618},{"x":0.083044973526340965,"w":0.69723185221354167,"y":0.51889433183666611,"h":0.016095171448565426,"c":1,"t":"The candidate and the examiner introduce themselves. Candidates then answer general"},{"x":0.082904644222690921,"y":0.53444323167563457,"t":"questions about themselves, their home\/family, their job\/studies, their interests and a wide","h":0.023374358618317825,"w":0.72172653198242187,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.081228591091667496,"w":0.6489341227213542,"t":"range of similar familiar topic areas. This part lasts between four and five minutes.","y":0.55389463754338397,"h":0.020414295023016615},{"y":0.58712386312463671,"h":0.01469559132260323,"c":1,"w":0.050173009236653632,"t":"Part 2","x":0.084775086990669712},{"w":0.7059735107421875,"h":0.019514651128343163,"c":1,"x":0.082993990884696126,"t":"The candidate is given a task card with prompts and is asked to talk on a particular topic.","y":0.60734849198374263},{"w":0.68176544189453114,"h":0.019609418592726691,"t":"The candidate has one minute to prepare and they can make some notes if they wish,","c":1,"x":0.081262149315159279,"y":0.62527964381889234},{"t":"before speaking for between one and two minutes. The examiner then asks one or two","h":0.019520739561365241,"y":0.64360740894564761,"c":1,"w":0.69040237426757822,"x":0.082996912448433588},{"t":"questions on the same topic.","w":0.23204065958658857,"x":0.08292063580558609,"h":0.017683453623275835,"c":1,"y":0.66408315440557086},{"y":0.69476744160074455,"t":"Part 3","x":0.084775086990669712,"w":0.050173009236653632,"h":0.014534884186538477,"c":1},{"x":0.082964644887064953,"h":0.021314971341879985,"c":1,"y":0.71410283692132837,"t":"The examiner and the candidate engage in a discussion of more abstract issues which","w":0.67838261922200527},{"t":"are thematically linked to the topic in Part 2. The discussion lasts between four and","h":0.023003657603280603,"y":0.73096700760027244,"w":0.65775817871093745,"c":1,"x":0.082900028577075305},{"w":0.1038062286376953,"h":0.014708814627645395,"c":1,"t":"five minutes.","y":0.75436046485925012,"x":0.08304498239972212},{"c":1,"h":0.019667303086661869,"t":"The Speaking test assesses whether candidates can communicate effectively in English.","w":0.69386906941731763,"x":0.082987621683363572,"y":0.78772837697284115},{"x":0.086505199077085329,"y":0.8081395349543099,"t":"The assessment takes into account Fluency and Coherence, Lexical Resource, Grammatical","h":0.015988371937820545,"c":1,"w":0.71799306233723958},{"t":"Range and Accuracy, and Pronunciation. More intormation on assessing the Speaking test,","c":1,"h":0.015988371937820434,"y":0.82703488378677548,"x":0.084775075679548784,"w":0.71972320556640623},{"x":0.082971863301111032,"w":0.62296381632486975,"h":0.020073007753130589,"t":"including Speaking assessment criteria (public version), is available at ielts.org.","c":1,"y":0.84358830089393211},{"t":"6","x":0.084775086721176979,"y":0.96075581424270717,"w":0.012110726038614905,"h":0.014534882851794828,"c":1}],"w":2400}